<file path="guide.html">
<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Guide | Boulder Inversion Tracker</title><body style="font:16px/1.6 system-ui;max-width:850px;margin:3em auto;padding:0 1em;background:#0f172a;color:#e2e8f0"><a style="color:#67e8f9" href="/">← Dashboard</a><h1>Reading the forecast</h1><p>The scenic and low-cloud indices are **not probabilities**. Scenic suitability looks for low cloud over Boulder, drying before summit elevation, and limited middle/high clouds. HRRR's total cloud top may represent upper-level clouds, and an RH drying transition is not a measured fog top.</p><p>The time slider changes only among forecasts you have actually downloaded. The mountain cross-section is illustrative. Multiple map locations can share HRRR's ~3 km grid cells.</p><h2>Forecast history</h2><p>Compare T−24, T−18, T−12, T−6 and T−0. T−0 is a model forecast available near the event time, not an observation. Captured predictions are distinct from later reconstructions. KBDU METAR reports are airport observations, not summit observations.</p><h2>Refresh</h2><p>Open the website and click Refresh everything, or run <code>python -m scripts.quicklook --refresh-only</code>. Historical downloads take longer on first retrieval. The XGBoost/CNN research pipeline is archived and not used by this website.</p><p>First Flatiron: 7,258 ft; Green Mountain: 8,133 ft.</p></body></html>
